             Dear {!Contact.FirstName},  <br /><br />

Thank you for your interest in the BFA in Dance and BFA in Dance Education at the School of Film, Dance and Theatre at Arizona State University!<br /><br />
 
Nationally recognized as among the best in the world, ASU's innovative dance programs have a unique emphasis on developing each student's creativity and individual movement practice.<br /><br />

ASU offers an interdisciplinary curriculum that promotes collaboration and building the skills necessary for a successful career in dance. With extraordinary course offerings in many different styles – from urban to postmodern contemporary to ballet – <b>the BFA in Dance</b> provides cutting edge dance training in the context of the liberal arts education. Through performance opportunities, master classes with world-renowned guest artists and careful guidance from ASU's accomplished dance faculty, students at ASU discover their unique goals as dancers and build towards fulfilling careers.<br /><br />

The ASU School of Film, Dance and Theatre also offers <b>BFA in Dance with a concentration in Dance Education.</b> All students pursuing this concentration complete the Professional Teacher Preparation Program (PTPP) through the ASU Mary Lou Fulton Teachers College and receive certification to teach in Arizona schools. In addition to the standard dance courses, students in this concentration complete education courses, two semesters of field experience and one semester of student teaching.<br /><br />

Whether you want to refine your individual style, delve into choreography and production, or share your passion for movement as an instructor, you can create a dance degree that meets your personal goals at the ASU School of Film, Dance and Theatre.<br /><br />

<b>Steps to Apply:</b>
<ul>
<li>You may begin your ASU application <a href="https://students.asu.edu/apply" target="_blank">here</a>. Admission to the BFA programs also requires an <b>interview/audition;</b> for more information about <b>upcoming Dance Interview Days</b>, click here. </li><br/>

<li>You must be admitted to Arizona State University as a "Dance Interview" major before you can interview for the BFA programs. Please <b>make sure that all of your materials are submitted</b> so that ASU can make an admission decision on your behalf prior to your interview date. </li><br/>

<li>If you pass your interview, your major will be changed to Dance. (In the event that you are admitted to ASU, but not selected for the Dance program, you will be placed in the second major choice you selected at the time of application. We recommend the BA in Performance and Movement, where you can continue your dance education. Students are allowed two interview attempts to enter the BFA programs and are responsible for communicating with the School to schedule a second interview.)</li>
</ul><br />

If you'd like to learn more, we hope you'll <a href="https://herbergerinstitute.asu.edu/forms/students/tours/index.php" target="_blank">visit campus</a> to check out our facilities and meet our students and faculty. You can also like our <a href="https://www.facebook.com/ASUFilmDanceTheatre" target="_blank">Facebook</a> page to stay up to date on upcoming events and announcements, see pics and video of our shows and hear what our amazing students are up to.

We look forward to welcoming you to campus! <br /><br />


Sincerely, <br />
 {!User.FirstName} {!User.LastName}
